        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): preserve tabs and newlines in prompt literal sanitization",
        "body": "Closes #105186\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users trying to pass untrusted source code or tab-separated data containing tabs and newlines into the prompt engine would experience completely broken formatting and destroyed indentation layout because `sanitizeForPromptLiteral` destructively stripped tabs and newlines.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe sanitization regex was configured to strip all Unicode control characters (`Cc` category), which includes tab (`\\t`) and newline (`\\n`). We added a negative lookahead `(?![\\t\\n])` to the regex in `src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.ts` to preserve these critical whitespace characters for code structure and layout.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCode formatting, tabs, and newlines are preserved when code blocks are sanitized and embedded into LLM prompts, ensuring that code indentation is maintained and prompts remain highly readable for the models.\n\n## Evidence\n\nUnit tests in `src/agents/sanitize-for-prompt.test.ts` were updated to assert that tabs and newlines are correctly preserved, while other control characters (CR, NUL) are still stripped:\n```typescript\n  it(\"strips ASCII control chars (CR/NUL) but preserves tabs and newlines\", () => {\n    expect(sanitizeForPromptLiteral(\"/tmp/a\\nb\\rc\\x00d\\te\")).toBe(\"/tmp/a\\nbcd\\te\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"preserves tabs and newlines for code fidelity\", () => {\n    expect(sanitizeForPromptLiteral(\"line1\\nline2\\tindented\")).toBe(\"line1\\nline2\\tindented\");\n  });\n```\nAll checks run successfully on Vitest.\n",
        "branch": "fix/105186-v2",
